  "body": "## Summary\n\nDependent draft after #385. Integrates updated core #331 and current observed main, preserving the full source history and later payment replay/recovery implementation. No provider activation or production deployment.\n\n- Reuse upstream Datafast automatic-debit confirmation compatibility and PayPal/public-checkout completion gates; do not invent a Datafast separate capture operation.\n- Repair the remaining shared capability gate for PlaceToPay bank redirects, DeUna, and PayPhone wallet: a method must qualify authenticated status lookup before it is offered or a new hosted session starts.\n- Add nine PostgreSQL-backed integration cases plus a pure normalization regression; preserve original intents, exact replay, marketplace restrictions, method-specific evidence and environment isolation.\n- Preserve upstream main changes, union reviewed catalog decisions, and regenerate inventory snapshots without weakening the catalog gate.\n- Add ADR 0126, exact test evidence, rollout/rollback guidance and the current staging-access blocker.\n\n## Dependencies and review order\n\nBase: #385 (`codex/payment-reconciliation-evidence-view-20260915`). Merge the existing dependent payment stack through #385 before this draft. Local integration commits include updated #331 at `a8d31238aaef8e919551c74010d6f8f820ac231a` and main at `0784958ecb8916106ab21ae3121f50893b71aefc`; both exact heads remained current at final fetch. No GitHub PR was merged.\n\nThe comparison includes already-reviewed upstream artwork/Instagram workflow changes because the base has older main ancestry. Review new payment code primarily in `ProviderCapabilities.hs`, `PaymentRuntimeStore.hs`, `Server/PaymentAvailability.hs`, and `ProviderRetrySpec.hs`. Keep the reviewed catalog-decision union and the later exact-method/idempotent continuation code.\n\nMobile #82 / gitlink `33720ef45b0565005c4b54b0e0c106cc93831613` is unchanged. No API shape, OpenAPI/generated client, native screen or new admin UI change; no screenshots produced.\n\n## Verified local tests\n\nRuntime/test source: `15831852417ea03e5d2db6204ffc463c3e4401e8`. Later commits change generated inventories/documentation only. Local macOS, Node 24.8, Stack lts-24.42/GHC 9.10.3, PostgreSQL 16.10. All provider fixtures/configuration synthetic.\n\n- Full backend: **2,603 examples / zero failures**, exit 0, 2026-09-16 02:45 UTC, original seed `1116919930`.\n- Fresh disposable PostgreSQL harness: **215 examples / zero failures**, whole harness exit 0, 02:47 UTC. Includes migration repeat apply, empty rollback/operator-seed preservation, reapply, used-history rollback refusal and history readability.\n- Web regression: **7 suites / 59 tests**, exit 0; production build/typecheck/preload budget passed.\n- Repository quality: **232 tests**, exit 0; zero critical/errors in formal checks. Existing 377 warnings / 9,386 informational findings retained.\n- Mobile canonical checkout: **3 tests**, exit 0; mobile typecheck passed; generated web/mobile types byte-identical. Not native/device QA.\n- Catalog gate: **1,430 files / 1,135 reviewed candidates**, no unreviewed/stale decisions; exit 0. `git diff --check` and new document relative-link checks passed.\n\nRetained failures, not hidden: the pre-fix DB run failed all three new status-query cases, proving the gap. The first full backend run had one unrelated onboarding evidence-window failure (`ServerSpec.hs:5451`); focused and full same-seed reruns passed unchanged. Its cause remains unproven; no assertion was weakened and no onboarding source changed. The first restricted DB attempt failed before writes; approved local-socket execution succeeded. The first post-fix DB log was green but its final exit was not retained, so the complete harness was repeated on another fresh database for definitive evidence.\n\nExact commands, timestamps, local log paths, commit mapping and limitations:\n[`docs/payments/stack-integration-2026-09-15.md`](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/codex/payment-stack-integration-20260915/docs/payments/stack-integration-2026-09-15.md).\nAll three disposable database servers stopped and verified stopped; synthetic data/logs retained.\n\n## Migration, configuration and rollback\n\nNo new SQL migration, backfill, provider account/capability seed, secret, feature flag or external transaction. Existing migration dependencies tested by the harness. Unqualified methods may disappear as intended: do not mark documented capabilities verified to force a checkout button to appear. Keep existing-operation recovery/reconciliation available; hiding a method never proves no charge or authorizes a cross-provider retry.\n\nApplication rollback must first disable new checkout for affected methods to avoid reintroducing underqualification. Preserve historical operation names, provider references, idempotency keys, intents, financial history and held-payment evidence. No data rollback required.\n\n## Blocked / unexecuted\n\nTwo staging inspector attempts on 2026-09-15 (including approved unrestricted retry) returned public HTTP 200 health but `hosting_authentication_unavailable` for all six hosting checks, `sourceCommit=null`, `providerQualified=false`. Restore authorized `FLY_STAGING_API_TOKEN` / `FLY_STAGING_WEB_TOKEN` or local Fly login, then qualify immutable deployment SHA, merchant sandbox aliases/contracts/secret names and registered webhooks. No credential values inspected or displayed.\n\nNo provider sandbox success, qualified staging deployment, live payment, refund, payout or production activation is claimed. Real provider completion/cancellation/replay/webhook/settlement tests, native QA, legal/accounting/PCI review, compliant seller payout execution, remaining recurring/refund/void/product fulfillment flows remain open. This is a tested integration repair, not completion of the entire payment platform.\n",
